"Let $k$-sun systems be decompositions of the complete graph $K_v$ into copies of the graph formed from a $k$-cycle by adjoining one pendant edge at each cycle vertex. The necessary conditions for such a system are\n\n$$\nv\\geq 2k\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad v(v-1)\\equiv 0 \\pmod{4k}.\n$$\n\n**Spectrum conjecture.** Let $k\\geq 3$ and $v>1$. There exists a $k$-sun system of $K_v$ if and only if\n\n$$\nv\\geq 2k\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad v(v-1)\\equiv 0 \\pmod{4k}.\n$$\n\nThe existence problem is completely settled for several values of $k$, including $k=3,5$, $k=4,6,8$, $k=10,14$, and powers of two at least $4$; a general result also establishes sufficiency when $v$ is sufficiently large relative to $k$. The conjecture asserts that the displayed necessary conditions are sufficient in every remaining case."